// Capabilities and the methods they map to:
//   plugin.checks  RunCheck
// A plugin that declares plugin.checks lists its checks in Manifest.checks. The host shows each as a button on the
// plugin's settings page and calls RunCheck only when an administrator presses it; checks never run on their own and
// never decide whether settings can be saved.
//
// A check is for confirming settings: that a key or account is accepted, that a source can be reached, how much quota
// is left. It must not download catalog data in bulk, write files, change the plugin's state or start other work. The
// host only shows the result text: it stores nothing, changes no settings and records no task. The host enforces a
// 30-second deadline, one running check per plugin and at most one run of the same check (for a per-item check, of
// the same check on the same entry) every 10 seconds.

